[rvn-ple] Remap NEXTN's draft to Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP for a grafted RVN text checkpoint

rvn-w4a16 only. Three gaps, all named in patch 0057's note as the day an
RVN checkpoint ships MTP layers, and the graft stamp is that day:

  * configs/model_config.py rewrote the draft architecture to
    Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP only for architectures[0] ==
    Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration, so a grafted text checkpoint built its
    draft worker as a second 48-layer copy of the target. The new branch
    mirrors the multimodal one exactly -- deep-copy the shared hf_config,
    collapse to one full_attention layer, num_nextn_predict_layers = 1,
    which is what sizes the draft KV pool in
    model_executor/model_runner_components/layer_setup.py -- and it is gated
    on the graft stamp through is_rvn_text_mtp_graft, so an unstamped RVN
    text launch is untouched.

  * arg_groups/speculative_hook.py defaulted the draft path to the target
    path only for the listed (multimodal and DeepSeek-family) archs, leaving
    speculative_draft_model_path None for the text arch: the draft worker in
    managers/tp_worker.py then had no directory to read. The default now
    also fires for a grafted text checkpoint, restricted to the resolved
    "EAGLE" algorithm -- the name --speculative-algorithm NEXTN arrives as --
    so EAGLE3/STANDALONE still require an explicit external draft path.

  * models/qwen3_5_mtp.py answered "BF16 MTP" for a grafted launch and the
    draft worker died on its first expert tensor: the grafted rvn-w4a16
    directory is a uniform W4A16_NVFP4 checkpoint, patch 0048 resolves
    --speculative-draft-model-quantization modelopt_mixed to modelopt_fp4
    for it, and the serialized-NVFP4 rule in _mtp_quant_config drops that
    config to None ("NVFP4" is a substring of "W4A16_NVFP4"). The draft
    FusedMoE was then built unquantized, and _load_w13 copied the packed
    [640, 1280] mtp.layers.0.mlp.experts.0.gate_proj.weight (intermediate
    640, hidden 2560 halved by the e2m1 packing) into a BF16 w13 narrowed
    to [640, 2560]: "size of tensor a (2560) must match the size of tensor
    b (1280) at non-singleton dimension 1". The multimodal launch never
    hits this because its mixed-precision quantized_layers map names the
    mtp.* layers and the rule keeps the config. The fix is a stamp-gated
    bypass: a draft config carrying patch 0058's graft stamp keeps the
    target's quantization -- the byte-identical copy is exactly the packed
    NVFP4 payload. The bypass keys on the stamp's own fields (frozen
    encoder_version, count 1), not on rvn_mtp_count, because the remap
    above leaves the draft's declared depth legitimately at 2
    (mtp_num_hidden_layers 1 plus num_nextn_predict_layers 1). The draft
    constructors and the shared-experts fusion gate run the same
    normalization, as the helper's own docstring demands.

The default is placed above rvn_text_bundled_draft_unsupported() on purpose:
that gate refuses a bundled NEXTN draft precisely because no draft path was
given, and for a grafted candidate there is one. Patch 0057 itself is
unmodified: an unstamped RVN text config still reaches the refusal, and a
grafted one reaches it as the pass-through branch it was written to have.

No weight-name mapping is needed on the draft side: Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP
inherits Qwen3_5ForCausalLMMTP.load_weights, which keeps only mtp-named
tensors and rewrites a top-level "mtp." to "model.", then "model.fc" to
"fc" and "model.pre_fc" to "pre_fc". Those are exactly the graft's names:
mtp.fc_embedding.weight and mtp.fc_hidden.weight land on the draft's
top-level fusion Linears, mtp.layers.0.mlp.experts.* land on the draft
FusedMoE as model.layers.0.mlp.experts.w13_weight (w1/w3 shards),
w13_weight_scale, w13_weight_scale_2, w2_weight, w2_weight_scale and
w2_weight_scale_2, mtp.layers.0.* otherwise land on its single
Qwen4ExpModel layer, and the draft needs no PLE table because
Qwen4ExpForCausalLMMTP clears config.ple_layer_ids itself
(models/qwen4_exp_mtp.py).

